  "summary": "The study fabricated free-standing electrospun Ti3C2Tx MXene/PAN mats, then stabilized and carbonized them to form binder-free Ti3C2Tx/carbon-nanofiber electrodes. Electrochemically discussed electrodes comprise the pure-carbon CNF8001 control and M10 composite fibers carbonized at 600 \u00b0C for 1 h, 700 \u00b0C for 1 h, 700 \u00b0C for 2 h, 800 \u00b0C for 1 h, and 700 \u00b0C for 6 h. M10CNF8001 delivered the highest explicitly sample-assigned value, 239 mF cm-2 at 10 mV s-1 in 1 M H2SO4; CNF8001 gave 75 mF cm-2 at the same scan rate. The conclusion also states an overall maximum of 244 mF cm-2, but does not assign that number and its measurement condition to a specific electrode. No areal mass loading, thickness, BET area, pore metrics, or electrode-specific gravimetric/volumetric capacitance was reported."
}